{
  "uid": "rio-castore-fuse",
  "title": "rio-build: Castore FUSE",
  "tags": ["rio-build", "builder", "castore-fuse"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {"from": "now-1h", "to": "now"},
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "FUSE upcalls by op",
      "description": "rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_upcalls_total[5m]) by op — the cold-metadata counter. With every cache TTL infinite, lookup/readdir fire ~once per distinct dentry per build (dcache + FOPEN_CACHE_DIR absorb repeats). A sustained op=read rate means passthrough is not engaging — cross-check the open() reply mode panel.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (op) (rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_upcalls_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{op}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "open() latency p50/p99",
      "description": "rio_builder_castore_fuse_open_seconds — open() upcall-to-reply. Bimodal by design: a backing-cache hit is one stat + one mountd round-trip (sub-ms); a remote fill is a whole-file ReadBlob bounded by jit_fetch_timeout. The hit=remote p99 isolates the fill tail.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_open_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_open_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_open_seconds_bucket{hit=\"remote\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99 (remote fill)",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "none"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "open() reply mode: passthrough vs keep_cache",
      "description": "rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_open_mode_total[5m]) by mode. passthrough = reads bypass FUSE entirely; keep_cache = userspace pread per uncached read. passthrough=0 with keep_cache>0 means FUSE_PASSTHROUGH was not negotiated — check the node kernel (>=6.9) and RIO_DISABLE_PASSTHROUGH.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 8, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (mode) (rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_open_mode_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{mode}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "open() dispatch case",
      "description": "rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_open_case_total[5m]) by case. hit = backing-cache hit (no fetch); miss_small = whole-file JIT fetch; miss_stream = above stream_threshold (streaming fill, P0575); wait_fetching = piggybacked on another open's in-flight fill. Rising miss share on repeat builds means the node cache is not retaining (P0571 LRU).",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 8, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (case) (rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_open_case_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{case}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "JIT fetch throughput by source",
      "description": "rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_fetch_bytes_total[5m]) by hit — bytes fetched on behalf of open(). hit=remote comes from rio-store; hit=node_ssd (shared node chunk cache) only appears once P0571/P0575 land. Compare against rio_builder_upload_bytes_total to see whether builders are input- or output-bound.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 16, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (hit) (rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_fetch_bytes_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{hit}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Fill chunks by source",
      "description": "rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_chunk_source_total[5m]) by src — where fill bytes came from. src=remote is rio-store; src=node_ssd (the shared /var/rio/chunks cache) appears with P0575. The node_ssd fraction is the cross-build dedup ratio.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 16, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (src) (rate(rio_builder_castore_fuse_chunk_source_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{src}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Integrity failures / EIO / fetch circuit",
      "description": "increase(rio_builder_castore_fuse_integrity_fail_total[5m]) — fetched bytes did not blake3-hash to the requested file_digest (corrupt store content or transport corruption; investigate immediately). increase(rio_builder_castore_fuse_eio_total[5m]) — EIO replies to the kernel; every one fails a build attempt as an infrastructure failure. rio_builder_castore_fuse_circuit_open — 1 when the fetch breaker is open (rio-store unreachable/degraded).",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 24, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(rio_builder_castore_fuse_integrity_fail_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "integrity failures (5m)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(rio_builder_castore_fuse_eio_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "EIO replies (5m)",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "max(rio_builder_castore_fuse_circuit_open)",
          "legendFormat": "fetch circuit open (any builder)",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {"mode": "thresholds"},
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "red", "value": 1}
            ]
          },
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 20, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "DAG prefetch latency p50/p99",
      "description": "rio_builder_castore_dag_prefetch_seconds — mount-time GetDirectory(recursive=true) Directory-DAG prefetch per build (one multi-root call for the whole input closure). Sustained p99 above ~10s delays every build start on the node — check rio-store GetDirectory latency and the directories table.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 24, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(rio_builder_castore_dag_prefetch_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(rio_builder_castore_dag_prefetch_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "none"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "rio-mountd request latency p99 by op",
      "description": "histogram_quantile(0.99, rio_mountd_request_seconds) by op — UDS request latency on the node-local mountd. backing_open/backing_close are a single ioctl (sub-ms), mount is a handful of syscalls, promote/promote_chunks copy+hash staged outputs (seconds for multi-GiB). backing_open p99 above ~1ms means mountd is CPU-starved on that node.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 32, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, op) (rate(rio_mountd_request_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{op}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "rio-mountd promote rejects by reason",
      "description": "rate(rio_mountd_promote_reject_total[5m]) by reason. reason=mismatch means a builder presented bytes that do not hash to the claimed digest — rio-store corruption or a compromised builder; identify the build_id in the mountd log and cross-check rio_store_narhash_mismatch_total. not-regular/too-large/race-timeout are protocol misuse or contention.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 32, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(rio_mountd_promote_reject_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "thresholds"},
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "red", "value": 0.001}
            ]
          },
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 20, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
